Comment: The application is linked against the LVGL based cp0_lvgl runtime of the
 CardputerZero launcher by M5Stack (Copyright M5Stack Technology CO LTD, MIT) and LVGL
 (Copyright LVGL Kft, MIT), which are part of the binary and are therefore listed in
 its Copyright field below. The fonts it draws with are the launcher's, read at run
 time from /usr/share/APPLaunch/share/font (Montserrat: SIL OFL 1.1; JetBrains Mono:
 SIL OFL 1.1; DejaVu Sans: the Bitstream Vera / DejaVu licence; Noto Sans CJK: SIL
 OFL 1.1, for Chinese, Japanese and Korean titles); none is shipped in this package.
 .
 The player engine, the queue, the folder browser, the tag readers (ID3, FLAC, Ogg,
 MP4, WAV and AIFF metadata), the WAV / AIFF reader, the media-key reader and the
 screens are the app's own code, written from the published format descriptions. The
 sound-server and ALSA layers and the FLAC and Ogg Opus readers are copied from the
 same repository's Cassette app (same author, MIT). The package holds no code of other
 music players and no codec code: every codec is a system library, loaded at run time.
 .
 Embedded cover pictures (JPEG, PNG) are decoded by stb_image v2.30 (Copyright 2017
 Sean Barrett and the stb contributors; public domain / MIT, either at your choice),
 one header compiled into the binary. LVGL's own lodepng (Copyright Lode Vandevenne,
 zlib licence) is also linked into the binary but the app does not use it.
 .
 Third-party libraries. None of the libraries below is part of this package: they are
 the system's own, provided by the OS packages named in the package's Depends and
 Recommends fields, which apt installs with it.
 .
 System libraries the binary is linked against at build time (named NEEDED in the
 binary): libfreetype6 (FreeType License or GPL-2.0-or-later), libinput10 (MIT),
 libxkbcommon0 (MIT), libstdc++6 and libgcc-s1 (GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime
 Library Exception 3.1). They are not copied into this package.
 .
 Libraries opened at run time with dlopen, only when the feature needs them, from the
 system when present; neither linked into the binary nor shipped in this package:
  - libmpg123.so.0 (mpg123, Copyright Michael Hipp, Thomas Orgis and the mpg123
    project; LGPL-2.1), for MP3. Package libmpg123-0t64.
  - libvorbisfile.so.3, with libvorbis and libogg (Copyright Xiph.Org Foundation;
    BSD-3-Clause), for Ogg Vorbis. Package libvorbisfile3.
  - libFLAC (Copyright 2000-2009 Josh Coalson, 2011 and later Xiph.Org Foundation;
    BSD-3-Clause), for FLAC. Package libflac14, libflac12t64 or libflac12.
  - libopus.so.0 (Copyright Xiph.Org, Skype Limited, Octasic, Jean-Marc Valin, Timothy
    B. Terriberry, CSIRO, Gregory Maxwell, Mark Borgerding, Erik de Castro Lopo,
    Mozilla, Amazon; BSD-3-Clause), for Opus. Package libopus0.
  - libasound.so.2, the ALSA library (alsa-lib, Copyright Jaroslav Kysela, Abramo
    Bagnara and others, LGPL-2.1-or-later), for the wired outputs of a board without a
    sound server. Package libasound2t64 or libasound2.
  - libpulse.so.0, the PulseAudio and PipeWire client library (PulseAudio, Copyright
    Lennart Poettering and others, LGPL-2.1-or-later), only when a sound server runs,
    for its outputs and Bluetooth audio. Package libpulse0.
  - FFmpeg: libavformat, libavcodec, libavutil and libswresample (Copyright the FFmpeg
    developers), only when a file needs them (AAC / ALAC / M4A, WMA, APE, WavPack and
    other formats), never at start-up. FFmpeg is LGPL-2.1-or-later upstream; Debian and
    Raspberry Pi OS build it with --enable-gpl, so the system libraries are
    GPL-2.0-or-later as built. Source: https://ffmpeg.org/ and the Debian source package
    "ffmpeg" (https://sources.debian.org/src/ffmpeg/). Packages libavformat61 (or 62),
    libavcodec61 (or 62), libavutil59 (or 60), libswresample5 (or 6), recommended: Vinyl
    works without them and says so when a file needs them.
 The licence texts of these libraries are in their own packages, under
 /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright.

